{"id":"h236","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? Penicillin was discovered by Louis Pasteur.","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"Louis Pasteur was a pioneer of microbiology.","confidence":0.95,"lean":0.1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"Pasteur's work on germ theory, fermentation, and vaccination laid groundwork for antibiotic research.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.2,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"In 1877 Pasteur and Joubert observed that airborne bacteria inhibited anthrax bacilli, an early sign of antibacterial effects.","confidence":0.85,"lean":0.2,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Some histories cite Pasteur's 1877 observation as a precursor to antibiotics.","confidence":0.7,"lean":0.2,"theta":1.0996,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Alexander Fleming discovered penicillin in 1928 when Penicillium mold killed Staphylococcus on a contaminated plate.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Florey and Chain later developed penicillin into a usable drug.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Pasteur's 1877 observation was general bacterial antagonism and did not identify or isolate penicillin.","confidence":0.92,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4451,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Pasteur's work was related and important but does not amount to discovering penicillin.","confidence":0.93,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4608,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The claim that Pasteur discovered penicillin is false.","confidence":0.96,"lean":-1,"theta":1.508,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":8,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":6,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":7,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":